      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Plasma beta-endorphin levels were found to be significantly lower in patients suffering from chronic pain of malignant etiology than in a control group. After a bilateral stereotactic cryothalamotomy in Centrum Medianum and Parafascicularis nuclei, a good clinical result and a significant increase in plasma beta-endorphin levels were obtained."},
